===Etymology===
{{rfe}}
1670s, from American Spanish, perhaps from a Carib word.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌbæɹəˈkuːdə/}}
* {{rhymes|uːdə}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|barracuda|barracudas}}

# Any large marine fish of the genus {{taxlink|Sphyraena|genus}} that have elongated bodies, a projecting lower jaw, displaying prominent fang-shaped teeth, and are aggressive predators.
# {{context|figuratively|lang=en}} An unethically predatory person.

